the 3ds had a significant hardware  upgrade this year but the best games for  Nintendo's enduring handheld play great  whether you're on a launch system or a  brand-new machine it's a testament to  the lasting appeal and versatility of  the handheld that you always have a  choice of both short and simple mobile  like fair and deep triple-a experiences  and that versatility is reflected in the  best 3ds games of 2015 despite monster  hunter's dominance in japan the series  has struggled to find similar success in  the West but this year's entry Monster  Hunter 4 ultimate goes a long way toward  rectifying what made earlier games in  the franchise so obtuse and  unapproachable it doesn't dump down the  combat but the main story progression  makes learning the game's robust battle  systems more accessible and even when  you're without a local or online partner  you're given some hearty feline  companions that make tackling even the  toughest beasts possible on your own  youkai watch fills the void left by a  year without a traditional Pokemon game  on its surface it may sound like just  another imitation of game freak's hit  series but the battle system sets yokai  watch a partner the active RPG combat  requires quick reflexes and active  monitoring of your party but you'll also  have to think about team layout and  balancing the abilities of your fighters  it might not replace Pokemon entirely  but it's a worthy alternative with a lot  of promise for future installments and  spin-offs  at first glance you might not guess that  the minimalistic box boy was created by  the same development studio behind the  colorful and majid ative kirby series  but box boys simple graphics balaiah  deep satisfying puzzle platformer your  abilities slowly expand but the gameplay  never becomes unnecessarily complicated  the puzzles require careful  consideration not split-second  button-pressing like any great puzzle  game it's true strength lies in giving  you seemingly insurmountable puzzles of  devilish complexity but also laying out  all the skills you need to solve them at  your fingertips  Triforce Heroes might seem like an odd  addition to our best 3 vs games list and  received an average score but it still  has moments of extreme excellence the  soundtrack is both original and totally  rich and the little graphical flourishes  in the game's backgrounds make you feel  like you're exploring a living  environment when you're playing with  friends Triforce Heroes captures the  adventure and puzzle solving elements  intrinsic to any great Zelda game it  isn't as much fun when playing solo and  the main adventure ends too quickly but  if you can find a party of dedicated  adventurers to brave the games dungeons  with this is still an epic quest  stretchmo reflects a very different  Nintendo from years past the fun solid  puzzle-solving builds off of earlier  games in the franchise but what sets  stretchmo apart is it's free to start  model stretchmo borrows the mobile like  business model that nintendo has  recently started implementing in more  games start for free pay to unlock more  content if you like it  games like stretch mode show how  Nintendo is bridging the gap between the  mobile and console worlds so that no  matter what gamers come out on top  it's been a great year for 3ds 2015 is  any indication we expect to see more of  the same mix of appealing games in  genres on 3ds going into the new year  and with the NX on the horizon might  even see Nintendo experimenting with  entirely new ways to play and enjoy  games on its popular handheld gaming  system  you
 

